course: dictionary
lesson: 7314
title: What is a placebo?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A placebo is a fake medicine. It looks like real medicine, such as a sugar pill, but it has no medicine in it. «A placebo is a dummy treatment with no active medicine.»
explain: Sometimes people feel better just because they believe they have been treated. This is called the placebo effect. The feeling is real, but the pill did not cure anything by itself.
explain: Why does this matter? «Scientists compare new medicines with placebos in trials to see if they really work.» One group gets the real medicine and another gets a placebo, so scientists can compare the results fairly.
fact: A placebo is a fake medicine, such as a sugar pill, with no medicine in it.
fact: The placebo effect is when someone feels better just because they believe they have been treated.
fact: In a fair test, one group gets the real medicine and another group gets a placebo.
fact: In a blind test, the people taking part often do not know which pill is real and which is the placebo.
exercise: What is a placebo? | A strong medicine that cures every illness | A test that takes a whole year | A doctor who works in a science lab | *A fake medicine, such as a sugar pill, with no medicine in it
exercise: «Scientists compare new medicines with placebos in trials.» Why do they do this? | To make the medicine taste nicer | To make the trial shorter | To stop people going to the doctor | *To see if the new medicine really works
exercise: What is the placebo effect? | The name of a famous doctor | A type of science test with no results | A medicine that makes you ill on purpose | *Feeling better just because you believe you were treated
test: In a science test, one group gets the real medicine and another gets a placebo. Why? | So the test finishes faster | So nobody needs a doctor | *So scientists can compare the two groups fairly | So the children get two lots of pills
test: In a blind test, what does blind mean? | *The people taking part often do not know who got the real medicine | The room has to be dark | Nobody can see the results on the screen | Only people who cannot see can take part
exam: Which sentence uses placebo correctly? | Her placebo was a long word for a happy dog | The placebo ran faster than the other children | *Scientists gave one group a placebo so they could compare the results | The placebo was a strong medicine that cured the cold in one day
